_:B2cb1cff1fe647352b534962cc000f6c3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#enrichment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Derived/decorative writer. Owns predicates produced by analysis, cross-references, computed metadata. Runs after the crawler; reads the crawler's structural-base, writes its own predicates without overlap." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#enrichment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "enrichment" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#enrichment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#crawler> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Structural-base writer. Owns predicates derived directly from filesystem state (path, sha, mtime, frontmatter values). Replaces-on-write per (class, identifier) tuple every crawl run." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#crawler> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "crawler" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#crawler> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Discriminator for chorus:writeOwner. Closed enum at this card; if a third writer ever lands (e.g. inference engine, human-curated overlay), it gets its own instance here and the validator's allow-list grows." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Writer" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writeOwner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Writer> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writeOwner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Required attribute on every predicate of a Hydratable class. Names which writer is responsible for this predicate's triples. Allowed values: chorus:crawler (predicate is structural-base, written from filesystem facts) or chorus:enrichment (predicate is derived, written by analysis/decoration). Two writers must never touch the same predicate." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writeOwner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "write owner" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writeOwner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hydratesFromSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hydratesFromSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Path glob (relative to CHORUS_ROOT) the crawler walks to populate instances of this class. Example: 'platform/scripts/*.sh' for chorus:Script. Annotation property on the class itself (not on instances), so the hydration validator does not require chorus:writeOwner here." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hydratesFromSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "hydrates from source" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hydratesFromSource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Hydratable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Marker class for any chorus class whose instances are populated from the filesystem by the crawler. Subclasses of chorus:Hydratable carry chorus:hydratesFromSource (where to read from) and have all their predicates declare chorus:writeOwner (which writer is responsible)." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Hydratable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hydratable" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Hydratable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
