<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hasSkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:Ba0ea29a73b4f99eb518b0018b4d69705 .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hasSkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A role or practice has a skill in its repertoire. Role hasSkill = the role's toolkit; Practice hasSkill = the named entry point that enacts the practice. #2348." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hasSkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has skill" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hasSkill> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#UtilitySkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Skill> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#UtilitySkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A skill that provides a utility action (open tab, share, listen, simplify, check-seeds, interrupt, cron-tick) and is not an enactment of a specific practice. Subclass exists so the orphan-skill query honestly excludes utilities: FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?s a chorus:UtilitySkill }. #2348 sub-spike 3A." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#UtilitySkill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Utility Skill" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#UtilitySkill> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-competing-implementations> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One concept, one implementation. When the same idea lives in multiple surfaces — two version sources, three drift detectors, three boot-enforcement attempts — they drift out of phase and nobody knows which is load-bearing. Root cause is weak APIs: when the contract is prose or convention instead of a callable surface, every new attempt adds a parallel implementation rather than replacing the prior one. Every new implementation must retire its predecessor; if you cannot retire it, the contract is not strong enough — fix the API first. The #2311 jenga pattern (5+ prior attempts at drift detection, none removed) is this principle's canonical violation." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-competing-implementations> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No competing implementations" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-competing-implementations> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
