<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ceremonyRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Practice> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ceremonyRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True on a practice that has no traceable principle — candidate for retirement or for naming the missing principle." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ceremonyRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ceremony risk" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ceremonyRisk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#operationalizes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#operationalizes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Practice> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#operationalizes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A practice operationalizes a policy — the concrete doing that the policy's binary rule sits inside. Practice → Policy. Zero or one per practice; a practice with no policy is voluntary." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#operationalizes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "operationalizes" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#operationalizes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#expresses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#expresses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Practice> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#expresses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A practice expresses (embodies, enacts) a principle. Practice → Principle. Counterpart to chorus:enforces (Policy → Principle) at the doing-layer." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#expresses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "expresses" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#expresses> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-tdd-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-speed-and-quality-correlate> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-tdd-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-tdd-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every code card must have failing tests (red) before production code is written. Enforced by tdd_gate.rs PreToolUse hook. DEC-1674." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-tdd-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TDD required before code" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-tdd-gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-quality-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-produce-no-waste> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-quality-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-quality-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Quality gate (hooks pass, no regression, no console.log in production code) must pass before /demo is called on a code card. Kade-owned. Enforced by /gate-quality skill + quality_gate.rs hook integration." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-quality-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quality gate required before demo" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-quality-gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-pair-enforcement> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-integrate-rather-than-segregate> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-pair-enforcement> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-comprehension-is-the-rate-limit> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-pair-enforcement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A /pair session has exactly one navigator and one driver. Navigator scopes; driver implements. Rotation checkpoints enforce turn-taking. Partner silence > 60s = stall signal (see policy-response-window-60s for the heartbeat). Enforced by /pair skill state + future pair-heartbeat-check skill (#2317)." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-pair-enforcement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pair has navigator + driver, not spectators" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-pair-enforcement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-nudge-blast-radius> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-focus-is-infrastructure> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-nudge-blast-radius> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-protect-attention> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-nudge-blast-radius> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A nudge targeting a role carries the card context (WIP id if present, reason for interruption). Cross-domain nudges surface a warning. DEC-107 dual-path persist+deliver is the mechanism; blast-radius is the discipline around when it fires." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-nudge-blast-radius> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nudge requires WIP context" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-nudge-blast-radius> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-icd-write-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-icd-write-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-dark-work> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-icd-write-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A harvester service file (harvest-*.sh, *-harvester.service.ts) cannot be written if the domain has no ICD provider section in urn:gathering:icd/current. Populate the ICD first, then code. DEC-095. Enforced by icd-gate-hook.sh PreToolUse hook." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-icd-write-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No harvester without ICD provider" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-icd-write-gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-handoff-logger> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-artifacts> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-handoff-logger> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-dark-work> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-handoff-logger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Briefs, nudges, gate-passes, and acceptances across roles must log to activity.md. If it's a handoff, it's traceable. Enforced by role discipline + future handoff-gate hook (not yet materialized)." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-handoff-logger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every cross-role handoff logged" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-handoff-logger> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-provenance> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-artifacts> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-provenance> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-dark-work> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-provenance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every demo produces a durable artifact (brief file or card comment) identifying what was shown, by whom, when. Verbal-only demos do not satisfy the demo gate. Enforced by demo_gate.rs hook reading comments/briefs — #2177 migrates fully to card comments." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-provenance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Demo evidence is an artifact" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-provenance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-apply-self-regulation-and-accept-feedback> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-dark-work> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A code card cannot be marked Done without demo evidence. Builder cannot self-accept. DEC-048 Proving Gate. Enforced by demo_gate.rs hook and /acp skill." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No accept without demo" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-demo-gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-accept-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-artifacts> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-accept-gate> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-no-dark-work> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-accept-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An acceptance must complete all four: move card to Done, emit card.accepted spine event, commit changes via git-queue, push. Partial acceptance is not acceptance. Enforced by /acp skill steps 1-4." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-accept-gate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accept = Done + spine + commit + push" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-accept-gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-use-edges-and-value-the-marginal> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#abstract> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Jeff lens reading of a principle as rendered on /book/principles-reconstructed.html. Free-text prose showing how Jeff models or demonstrates the principle in practice. #2447." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "jeff reading" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Tech/Chorus lens reading of a principle as rendered on /book/principles-reconstructed.html. Free-text prose that operationalizes the principle for team + engineering context. #2447." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tech/chorus reading" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-small-scale-intensive-systems> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every Chorus service works every time (reliable), declares its edges (bounded), and behaves the same until deliberately versioned (idempotent unless changed). Enforcement — gates, hooks, contracts, tests, types — exists in service of these properties, not as an end in itself." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Services are reliable, bounded, and idempotent" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A service writes state to a persistence or emits events consumed by another service. Distinguishes data production from data consumption at the service level. #2178." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "writes" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#writes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#reads> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A service reads state from a persistence or another service. Read-only, no mutation. #2178 — turns the Athena envelope from labels into a graph an agent can traverse." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#reads> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reads" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#reads> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
