<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#loom-policies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Team policies — working hours, WIP limits, response windows." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#loom-policies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Policies" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#loom-policies> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#SubDomain> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-chorus-search-first> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-chorus-search-first> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Search order: Chorus (/chorus search) → codebase graph → filesystem (Grep/Glob). Guard hook enforces. DEC-074." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-chorus-search-first> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Chorus search before filesystem" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-chorus-search-first> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-self-acp> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-self-acp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only Wren or Jeff can accept. The builder CANNOT mark their own code card Done. DEC-048 Proving Gate." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-self-acp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No self-accept on code cards" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-self-acp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-response-window-60s> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-protect-attention> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-response-window-60s> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If your pair partner completes an AC item, you respond within 60 seconds. If you can't, emit a status (thinking, blocked on X). Silence = stall. DEC-1571 Attention Contract." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-response-window-60s> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "60-second pair heartbeat" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-response-window-60s> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-raw-process-kill> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-services-reliable-bounded-idempotent> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-raw-process-kill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Never `kill` PIDs directly, local or remote. Use launchctl kickstart for LaunchAgents, app-state.sh for the Gathering app lifecycle. LaunchAgent changes route through Silas." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-raw-process-kill> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No raw process killing" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-no-raw-process-kill> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-working-hours> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-protect-attention> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-working-hours> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Default working window is 6am–8pm Boston time. Jeff's direction always overrides: do not question off-hour requests, do not ask Jeff about working-hour boundaries. The window is for self-initiated agent work when no direction has been given; when direction exists, execute it regardless of clock." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-working-hours> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Working window 6am–8pm Boston" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#policy-working-hours> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Practice> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A practice or policy traces back to the principle(s) that motivate it." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "derived from" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#derivedFrom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A binary team rule — allowed/blocked, in-bounds/out-of-bounds. Derived from principles but enforceable as yes/no (unlike practices, which are disciplines). Examples: working hours, WIP limits, response windows, touch-count targets." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Policy" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Policy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#dependsOn> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#spine-service> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#dependsOn> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#gates-service> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#kade> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Horizontal quality discipline — test pyramid, coverage measurement, gates, test-value policy. Defines what 'works' means for Chorus and enforces it at the right moments. Measurement + model; enforcement is other sub-products consuming it (assembler-not-generator shape, same as Pulse and Roles)." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quality" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#quality-product> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#SubProduct> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-interrogate-the-data> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-interrogate-the-data> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Interrogate the data you touch before repeating or acting on it. Every claim you relay is a claim you own. Check provenance, verify fossils, refuse to narrate over gaps. The failure mode is storytelling — coherent-sounding prose that papers over what the data actually shows." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-interrogate-the-data> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Give a fuck about data quality" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-interrogate-the-data> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-comprehension-is-the-rate-limit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-comprehension-is-the-rate-limit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The team's real throughput is set by what can be understood, not what can be generated. Output beyond the rate of comprehension is debt disguised as speed. You own what you understand, not what you produced." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-comprehension-is-the-rate-limit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Comprehension is the rate limit" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-comprehension-is-the-rate-limit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-speed-and-quality-correlate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-biological-renewable-resources> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-speed-and-quality-correlate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Speed and quality both come from uninterrupted thinking — they are not a trade-off. Skipping review does not produce speed; it produces rework plus the interruption load that rework generates." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-speed-and-quality-correlate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Speed and quality correlate" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-speed-and-quality-correlate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Build quality in at construction, not at inspection. No staging means the shortcut that skips thinking is the bug that costs more than the thinking would have." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quality at the source" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-quality-at-source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-focus-is-infrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-biological-renewable-resources> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-focus-is-infrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Focus windows are infrastructure, not preference. Every interruption has a cost; make the cost visible. Interruption is a last resort, not a default." .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-focus-is-infrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Focus is infrastructure" .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principle-focus-is-infrastructure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#Principle> .
